    {
      "id": "claim_37601233ec524e8db80f487314af35d8",
      "statement": "Moving or adding a prod published port also requires updating that port's self-referencing URL var, because the collision gate only scans the compose `ports:` key: concretely KC_HOSTNAME_ADMIN — set to the :19099 admin URL by the prod-auth stack's `environment` block in infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml and required fail-fast as ${KC_HOSTNAME_ADMIN:?} by the keycloak prod compose — and LangFuse's own NEXTAUTH_URL login/callback URL in the observability prod compose. Missing this leaves a working port bind pointing at a stale URL that no port-scan gate can see.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/keycloak/compose.prod.yaml#L70-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:25b4078f6b1d60989f3169dba0eae7fb38de94c85c08ab9d8c2314fd81f9fe98:"
        },
