    {
      "id": "claim_63a799f779f54460a0f08b084f470692",
      "statement": "The prod-auth stack's environment block in infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml no longer passes KC_ADMIN_BIND_IP to the keycloak prod compose (removed 2026-10-12, item #727) and instead carries KC_HOSTNAME_ADMIN=http://[[TAILNET_HOST]]:19099. While it was passed, Komodo wrote KC_ADMIN_BIND_IP into .env.prod, which the keycloak prod compose loads with `env_file:`, so it reached the container as a KC_* variable that names no Keycloak option — the admin URL has always used the separate KC_HOSTNAME_ADMIN, which is the live var a port move must keep in sync.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md",
